  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In Gu Yue Village only one inn sells green bamboo wine, while three taverns sell common rice wine, muddy wine, and similar cheap liquor. A jar costs two primeval stones, about two months of ordinary household expenses. When uncorked, a refreshing and mellow fragrance fills the room.",
      "chapters": [
        12
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "village-specialty",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_gu_yue_village"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Green bamboo wine is called the Gu Yue Village’s number one wine. Fang Yuan drips it through the bamboo forest at night so its aroma can draw a Liquor worm.",
      "chapters": [
        13
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "liquor-worm-bait",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_liquor_worm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration calls the wine really rich and the best on Qing Mao Mountain, and credits its aroma as the biggest reason the Liquor worm comes to Fang Yuan that night.",
      "chapters": [
        16
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "best-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A jar supports a Liquor worm for about four days. The worm can live on turbid wine or rice wine, but those second-rate wines demand many jars each day, so Fang Yuan buys green bamboo wine instead as both thrift and cover. The inn’s stock is limited; caravans conventionally buy it out, which threatens long-term feeding if jars run short.",
      "chapters": [
        23
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "feeding-cost",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a caravan visit the inn sells out. Fang Yuan takes rice wine for the moment and pre-orders a hundred jars of the next brew.",
      "chapters": [
        64
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seasonal-stock",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Together with Bai village’s white grain liquid and Xiong village’s bear gall wine, Gu Yue green bamboo wine is named among the three wines of Qing Mao.",
      "chapters": [
        117
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "three-wines-of-qing-mao",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_bai_village",
        "loc_xiong_village",
        "fac_gu_yue_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Zheng later calls the same specialty bamboo wine and says the sole village inn is the only place that sells it.",
      "chapters": [
        177
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-name",
